{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the complete document-only Source f9fbdac923f8313bb2bf8aa22f562dcaeefcd2c8, tree56cea3759b3480920470454625ab1fe5d9436de8. One remaining finding, all findings together below.\n\nF7 — P2: give commanded and reported device state distinct places in the design. Section3 says “A device item's state is the commanded state, not the physical one.” Section6.1 then lists one device state (open/closed/on/off/error), describes error as written by sensors, and calls report-device a transition that sets reported state while set-vent/set-fan/set-heater set commanded state. There is no consistent statement of which of these is the item's native state and which is a separate value. For example, after the operator commands heater2 off and before an observation confirms it, a delayed report of on must be able to record that fact without turning the commanded target back on or standing for a new command. Likewise, the error guard must read reported error without erasing the last commanded target.\n\nPlease name the distinct commanded and reported facts in the item sketch and say which each act may change and which the error guard reads. This can be a short design clarification, not a new schema or implementation: retain one error state with a descriptive failure, preserve separate owner outcome and sensor evidence, and keep the operator as signer of the heater command. Align section3, the device item/acts paragraph in6.1 and the fault story. An explicit choice of native state plus a value, or separate values with an explained native lifecycle, is enough. The change fixes the ambiguity introduced while resolving the earlier outside-effect finding.\n\nPrior findings disposition: F1 is answered by the explicit M2 features, per-slice dependencies, trusted pre-M2 G1 sketch and separate device-owner/custody prerequisites, without moving plan032's order. F2's fixed grants, kind guards, operator-signed authorize and bounded command-owner/outcome chain are answered; F7 concerns the resulting device representation, not a request for another authority mechanism. F3 now correctly makes reads/signing host-enforced, the grid's read-only rule future host work, and M1 trusted-only. F4 now correctly makes observe an input-only comment and report-device a guarded transition. F5 correctly withdraws the traffic-based guarantee, separates already-funded work from future acts and leaves retention/admission policy future work. F6 derives context and fallback from the displayed revision/state with the waiting map. The earlier error-state change remains reasonable.\n\nCoverage: primary2a19a419 read FIRST and FULL,534 lines, plus the complete delta from20a. One fresh, unretired, nonstale binding, remaining0. Independent Git leaf comparison shows all1980 reviewed Maindf806 leaves mode/type/blob exact and only this note added (1981 leaves). All19 local link occurrences resolve at that Main baseline; the archive anchor was checked in the prior review and is unchanged. Whitespace passes. I checked the relevant current ActType.grant, comment-validator, operation-driver attempt/outcome rules, applications M1/M2 and presentation boundary, plan032 and use-case catalogue. Earlier full guide/ten-terms and approved cards/views context carries by exact identity. A broad supplemental search was truncated; the decisive operation-driver and applications/plan passages were subsequently read in bounded untruncated output. No private prototype was accessed.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: the dependency, comment/projection and outside-owner direction is sound, but device command versus observation needs F7's explicit separation before the described definition/scenario can be authored unambiguously.\n\nSecurity conclusion: the fixed grants and host-enforced boundary resolve the earlier authority problems. F7 must preserve that a sensor can report evidence without modifying an operator's commanded target, and that a successful command transition never proves a physical effect. No claim of a safe arbitrary-package host, real-device run or custody implementation is accepted.\n\nSimplification conclusion: retain one generic card/view sketch and one bounded command owner, with separate intent, outcome and observation. Resolve the representation in a few precise sentences; no failure taxonomy, new grant mechanism, second platform or runtime change is needed.\n\nNote fidelity and honest evidence: this is an uncommissioned fictional design after the journey exit. The JSON is a future view sketch, not a runtime schema. Prototype observations remain attributed to one desktop app/stand-in host and do not prove phones, multiple people, push updates, devices or media custody. The note explicitly says no dap runtime run. Document-only handling under docs/testing.md: link/tree/whitespace review, no gate or repeated suite. Prior ddac358a and64cb435 changes-requested verdicts remain valid history; no approval or landing for this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2a19a419444d2b86b39040e5280ded88003a47ff","binding":"assigned","head":"f9fbdac923f8313bb2bf8aa22f562dcaeefcd2c8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:58f09910dcacb970356df4a9c84832c51f93c7c2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:00fa3165e633246022d5ef040a093d813150b72d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2f26d04ede3343a86bd43f3ee5f03d1d7c3229a2","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}